From d86efb2b57d61cc219a9e7ccd2482cf00abd813a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Thu, 24 Apr 2025 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] product: Exclude AOSP sample APN list from GSI build

The AOSP sample APN database (device/sample/etc/apns-full-conf.xml)
is explicitly a placeholder. Google's own documentation states there
is "no change in the behavior of Android devices" from it — Pixel
phones use their own CarrierSettings protobuf data instead.

Our build ships a comprehensive merged APN database derived from
Google Pixel CarrierSettings, AOSP IMS entries, and LineageOS
community data, installed via device/phh/treble/base.mk. The AOSP
sample file should not be installed alongside it, as it would be
ignored anyway (the merged file takes priority via PRODUCT_COPY_FILES).

This matches the approach taken by TrebleDroid and other custom
GSI builds.

Change-Id: I76c8d5ef67de73d4558d350a87a9bc317aaad792
---
 target/product/gsi/Android.bp | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/target/product/gsi/Android.bp b/target/product/gsi/Android.bp
index a61d544..a57e4a3 100644
--- a/target/product/gsi/Android.bp
+++ b/target/product/gsi/Android.bp
@@ -125,7 +125,6 @@ android_filesystem_defaults {
         "Dialer",
         "LatinIME",
         "Messaging",
-        "apns-full-conf.xml",
         "frameworks-base-overlays",
     ],
     multilib: {